    "introduction": "India, the seventh largest country in the world by area (3.287 million sq km, accounting for 2.4% of the world's land surface), lies entirely in the Northern and Eastern Hemispheres. Extending from 8\u00b04' N (Kanyakumari) to 37\u00b06' N (Indira Col) latitude, and from 68\u00b07' E (Ghuar Mota, Gujarat) to 97\u00b025' E (Kibithu, Arunachal Pradesh) longitude. The Indian Standard Meridian (82\u00b030' E), determining Indian Standard Time (IST = UTC + 5:30), passes through Mirzapur (near Prayagraj) in Uttar Pradesh.",
    "detailedExplanation": "<h3>1. Astronomical Extent & Extreme Geographical Points</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Latitudinal Extent:</strong> Mainland extends from <strong>8\u00b04' N</strong> (Cape Comorin / Kanyakumari, Tamil Nadu) to <strong>37\u00b06' N</strong> (Indira Col, Ladakh). The southernmost point of the Republic of India is <strong>Indira Point</strong> (formerly Pygmalion Point) at <strong>6\u00b045' N</strong> on Great Nicobar Island (partially submerged in 2004 tsunami).</li>\n  <li><strong>Longitudinal Extent:</strong> From <strong>68\u00b07' E</strong> (Ghuar Mota / Sir Creek, Kutch, Gujarat) to <strong>97\u00b025' E</strong> (Kibithu in Anjaw district, Arunachal Pradesh). The longitudinal span of ~30\u00b0 results in a 2-hour sun time difference between Arunachal Pradesh and Gujarat.</li>\n  <li><strong>Standard Meridian of India (82\u00b030' E):</strong> Passes through <strong>Mirzapur (near Prayagraj, UP)</strong>, and traverses 5 states: <strong>Uttar Pradesh, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Odisha, and Andhra Pradesh</strong>. IST is 5 hours and 30 minutes ahead of Greenwich Mean Time (GMT + 5:30).</li>\n  <li><strong>Tropic of Cancer (23\u00b030' N):</strong> Divides India into almost two equal halves, passing through 8 states: <strong>Gujarat, Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Tripura, and Mizoram</strong>. (Note: Does NOT pass through Uttar Pradesh).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. International Land Frontiers & Maritime Zones</h3>\n<p>India shares 15,106.7 km of land borders with 7 sovereign countries: <strong>Bangladesh (4,096.7 km, longest)</strong>, China (3,488 km), Pakistan (3,323 km), Nepal (1,751 km), Myanmar (1,643 km), Bhutan (699 km), and Afghanistan (106 km in Wakhan corridor). Total coastline: 7,516.6 km (mainland 5,422.6 km + islands 2,094 km). Under UNCLOS:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Territorial Waters:</strong> 12 nautical miles from baseline (full sovereign jurisdiction).</li>\n  <li><strong>Contiguous Zone:</strong> 24 nautical miles (customs, fiscal, immigration, sanitation enforcement).</li>\n  <li><strong>Exclusive Economic Zone (EEZ):</strong> 200 nautical miles (exclusive rights to explore, exploit, and conserve marine living and non-living resources).</li>\n</ul>",
